h('How the code is kept readable')
p('Prettier formats source consistently. Components separate presentation from server actions and storage helpers. Comments explain boundaries such as draft privacy, media cleanup and session invalidation rather than repeating every line. TypeScript checks shape compatibility; it does not replace runtime validation.')
code('npm run format\nnpm run format:check\nnpm run lint')
p('The script named lint currently runs tsc --noEmit, not a separate ESLint ruleset. Keep package-lock.json with the source so installs use the expected dependency versions.')

page('04 / First local setup')
step(1,'Prepare prerequisites','Install a compatible Node.js runtime and npm. Start the MySQL service in XAMPP. Next.js runs as a Node.js process; XAMPP Apache does not serve this app and is not required for the Next.js dev server. phpMyAdmin may use Apache for its own interface.')
step(2,'Open the project terminal','Use the repository root, not a parent folder. Install the locked dependencies with npm ci when package-lock.json is present. Use npm install when intentionally resolving or adding dependencies.')
code('npm ci')
step(3,'Configure environment variables','If .env already exists, preserve it. Otherwise copy .env.example to .env and replace placeholders. Use the actual MySQL user/password and database name. Local root without a password is not an acceptable production configuration.')
code('DATABASE_URL="mysql://USER:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:3306/di_recruitment"\nAUTH_SECRET="REPLACE_WITH_A_RANDOM_SECRET_32_OR_MORE_CHARACTERS"\nADMIN_EMAIL="your-admin@example.com"\nADMIN_PASSWORD="REPLACE_WITH_A_STRONG_UNIQUE_PASSWORD"')
p('Percent-encode special characters in URL credentials. Generate a random secret locally; never paste it into public documentation or commit it. Example generator:')
code('node -e "console.log(require(\'node:crypto\').randomBytes(32).toString(\'hex\'))"')
step(4,'Create tables and initialize','For a new local install, apply the Prisma schema, generate the client and run the seed. Review database-change warnings; do not accept data-loss prompts on a database you need.')
code('npm run db:push\nnpx prisma generate\nnpm run db:seed\nnpm run dev -- --port 3001')
p('Visit http://localhost:3001 and /admin/login. Use the initial account configured in .env only if it was newly created. An existing account may have a different password after an admin password change.')

page('05 / Seed, restart & daily commands')
h('What seed means in this project')
p('The seed script is a starter-data script, not the database itself. It upserts four sample jobs by slug and creates an initial administrator if configured. Existing admin accounts are preserved with an empty update object, so rerunning seed does not reset their password. Sample job fields can be overwritten on rerun; do not use seed as a routine repair command.')
table([['Command','When to use it'],['npm run dev -- --port 3001','Start local development. Keep this terminal running.'],['npm run db:push','Synchronize a local schema. Review risk before applying.'],['npx prisma generate','Regenerate Client after schema/provider changes.'],['npm run build','Generate Prisma Client, compile Next.js and check types.'],['npm start -- --port 3001','Run the already-built app; production mode needs HTTPS for secure admin cookies.'],['npm run lint','Run TypeScript checks without emitting files.'],['npm run format:check','Check formatting without changing files.']])
h('Safe schema-change restart on Windows')
p('Stop only this project\'s dev server with Ctrl+C. Apply reviewed schema changes, run prisma generate, then restart. An active Node process can lock Prisma\'s Windows engine DLL. Do not kill unrelated Node processes, erase node_modules blindly, or reset the database to solve a file lock.')
code('npx prisma db push --skip-generate\nnpx prisma generate\nnpm run dev -- --port 3001')
p('Avoid running two development servers against the same .next output directory. If port 3001 is occupied, identify the process and check which app owns it before stopping anything. A changed port means your old browser URL may point at another instance.')

page('06 / Public navigation & homepage')
